@startuml CampusDesk escalation activity
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundCorner 8
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #FAFAFA
  BorderColor #444444
  DiamondBackgroundColor #DDE7F0
  DiamondBorderColor #444444
}

title Escalation process of one ticket

start
:Reporter submits a ticket;
:Ticket is routed to the team that owns the service;

if (Primary on call holds\nfewer than 3 tickets?) then (yes)
  :Assign to the primary;
elseif (Secondary on call holds\nfewer than 3 tickets?) then (yes)
  :Assign to the secondary;
else (no)
  :Ticket waits: Open, unassigned;
  :Notify the team lead (first waiting ticket)\nor the administrator (second and later);
  :Wait until someone on call has room\n(checked every minute, oldest ticket first);
  :Assign to that solver;
endif

:Status = Assigned, ticket is at tier 1\nClock starts (escalation_timer_started_at)\nSolver notified in the app and by email;

while (Every minute the server runs\n**manage.py escalate**.\nIs the ticket still Assigned?) is (yes)
  if (Time at this tier >=\ntier wait x severity factor?) then (yes)
    if (Does a later tier name a person who is active,\non the team, holds fewer than 3 tickets\nand is not the current holder?) then (yes)
      :Assign to that tier's person\nClock starts again\nTimeline records who and how long\nOnly the new solver is notified;
    else (no)
      #FFCFCA:Policy ran out\nStatus = Open, unassigned, flagged\nShown in red, first in the incident list\nTeam lead notified\n(administrators if the team has no active lead);
      stop
    endif
  else (no)
    :Nothing changes;
  endif
endwhile (no, the solver\nmoved it to In Progress)

:Clock stops, the ticket is never escalated again\nReporter notified: work started;
:Solver resolves the ticket\nReporter notified: resolved;
stop

floating note right
  Severity factor on every wait:
  critical 0.5, high 0.75, medium 1, low 2

  A reopened ticket, and a ran-out ticket the
  lead reassigns, start again at tier 1
  with a fresh clock.
end note

@enduml
